SUMMARY:Frederick City Market
DESCRIPTION:The Frederick City Market is a local food and artisan market located in the historic district of Downtown Frederick\, Maryland. Join us on every Sunday from May through November. Parking is free on Sundays and there are usually plenty of spots on 7th Street and Market Street. You can park at Gravel and Grind (15 E 6th Street) and walk through the gap into the market lot.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/frederick-city-market/11348/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventgreenburialswithmichaeljudd26051-20261004@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261004T151650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Green Burials with Michael Judd
DESCRIPTION:Are you curious about Home Funeral and Green Burial practices/options in Maryland? Join Michael Judd as he invites you to consider choices for end-of-life care\, home funeral\, home burial\, and green burial practices. Michael will share information\, resources\, and personal experiences as he honors the wise traditions of natural burial and the relevance of these choices for us today. Take a virtual tour of the Morris Orchard\, Frederick county’s first natural burial site which is centered in a chestnut orchard in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains. Michael Judd has worked with agro-ecological and whole-system designs throughout the Americas for over two decades\, focusing on applying permaculture and ecological design. His projects increase local food security and community health in both tropical and temperate growing regions. He is the founder of Ecologia Edible & Ecological Landscape Design\, Project Bona Fide\, an international nonprofit supporting agro-ecology research\, co-founder of SilvoCulture\, a Maryland based nonprofit which is helping plant 1 million nut trees in the Mid-Atlantic region\, and Morris Orchard Natural Burial. He is also the author of Edible Landscaping with a Permaculture Twist\, and For the Love of PawPaws. Michael lives with his family on a permaculture homestead nestled along the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains near Frederick\, Maryland. The Judds’ homestead consists of 25 acres of mixed woodlands\, food forests\, gardens\, and a nursery designed for experimentation and education.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/green-burials-with-michael-judd/26051/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261004@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261004T151650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
