BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmountolivetcemeteryhistory26mysterytour25242-20261011@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261004T151650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Mount Olivet Cemetery History & Mystery Tour
DESCRIPTION:Discover Frederick’s Past as we Navigate through the Labyrinth of Graves\, Crypts and Monuments of Historic Mount Olivet Cemetery. One of Maryland’s Largest and most Beautiful Cemeteries. Final Resting Place of Francis Scott Key\, Author of our National Anthem\, the Star Spangled Banner\; Maryland's first Governor\, Thomas Johnson and Civil War Heroine\, Barbara Fritchie. Tour also includes Intriguing Facts about the Cemetery’s Origin\, Tombstone Design\, Grave Robbing\, Mass Graves\, plus stops at other Distinctive Burial Plots\, including Revolutionary War\, War of 1812 and Civil War. Tour concludes with a visit to the Key Memorial Chapel. Reservations Required. (This is Not a Ghost Tour)
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/mount-olivet-cemetery-history-%26-mystery-tour/25242/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpourhousetriviaatsandboxbrewhouse23336-20261012@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261004T151650Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:Pour House Trivia at Sandbox Brewhouse
DESCRIPTION:Monday nights presented by Pour House Trivia are so ON! Every Monday\, 7-close. Bring a friend\, grab a beer\, and be prepared to test your knowledge with your host\, Ian\, from Pour House Trivia.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pour-house-trivia-at-sandbox-brewhouse/23336/
END:VEVENT
